\section{Why these are exported}{

Section 9.7 of the design rules gives the unavailability of these
helpers outside \code{pharos} as the reason \verb{plot.Desc.*} methods live in
\code{pharos} rather than next to the classes they plot. That reason no
longer holds. The placement of the existing methods is unchanged - the
export only removes the constraint, it does not itself relocate
anything.
}

\section{Contract for callers outside pharos}{

The rules in sections 9.1-9.5 apply unchanged: no direct \code{par()} call
outside \code{.applyParFromDots()}, \code{stamp} passed to
\code{.withGraphicsState()} rather than drawn by hand, no \code{oma}/\code{omi} in any
save/restore list, and no internal \code{mfrow}.
}

